================================================================================
UPSTREAM
================================================================================

Upstream ComfyUI-GGUF (City96, Apache-2.0) provides, and this fork reuses
unchanged:

  ops.py                  GGML custom operations and GGMLTensor
  dequant.py              dequantisation kernels for the ggml block formats
  loader.py               GGUF readers, image/sd.cpp compatibility mode, the
                          T5 / Llama / Gemma3 / Qwen2VL / Qwen3VL key maps,
                          tokenizer reconstruction
  tools/                  model -> GGUF conversion and llama.cpp quantization
                          helpers (convert.py, lcpp.patch, fix_5d_tensors.py,
                          read_tensors.py, fix_lines_ending.py)
  LICENSE                 Apache License 2.0, reproduced unmodified

  Upstream also provides nodes.py (the V1 node classes and GGUFModelPatcher).
  This fork is V3-only and does NOT reproduce those classes; the V1 schema is
  available from upstream itself. See "CHANGES MADE IN THIS FORK" below.

Upstream project: https://github.com/city96/ComfyUI-GGUF

================================================================================
CHANGES MADE IN THIS FORK (2026, IKBlue)
================================================================================

As required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b), modified files state that they were
changed. The complete list of modifications follows.

  qwen35_support.py  (NEW FILE, Copyright 2026 IKBlue)
      Qwen3.5 ("qwen35") text-encoder support.

      convert_qwen35()
          Remaps a raw qwen35 GGUF onto ComfyUI's native qwen35 checkpoint
          layout: llama.cpp -> comfy key renaming, the RMSNorm +1 centring
          offset, the ssm_a -> A_log log transform, the value-head channel
          permutation, and the conv1d channel-group order. Tensors are
          dequantised on return so load_state_dict sees real storage shapes.

      vision_from_mmproj()
          Converts a Qwen3.5 mmproj GGUF (llama.cpp vision tower) into
          ComfyUI's model.visual.* layout, for text encoder GGUFs that were
          exported language-only.

  nodes_v3.py  (NEW FILE, Copyright 2026 IKBlue)
      All six nodes re-expressed against the ComfyUI V3 schema
      (comfy_api.latest: io.ComfyNode / io.Schema / comfy_entrypoint), plus the
      GGUFCustomNodesExtension and comfy_entrypoint(). Derived from the
      corresponding V1 classes in upstream nodes.py.

  gguf_patcher.py  (NEW FILE, upstream City96 code relocated by IKBlue)
      GGUFModelPatcher and update_folder_names_and_paths, moved verbatim out of
      the upstream nodes.py so they stay separate from the node-schema module.
      The *_gguf folder registration is performed here at import, so it happens
      regardless of import order. Neither definition was altered.

  loader.py  (MODIFIED, upstream City96)
      + "qwen35" added to TXT_ARCH_LIST
      + an early qwen35 branch in gguf_clip_loader()
      + an optional vision_path argument that merges the mmproj vision tower
      + a mismatch guard rejecting a vision file that shares keys with the
        text encoder

  nodes.py  (REMOVED, upstream City96)
      The upstream V1 node classes were deleted when this fork became V3-only.
      The shared loading logic they used to carry (the CLIP state-dict reader,
      the text-encoder builder, the file-list and CLIPType helpers) was carried
      over into nodes_v3.py as module-level functions; GGUFModelPatcher and the
      folder registration went to gguf_patcher.py. The V1 classes themselves are
      not reproduced anywhere. Upstream remains the reference for V1 (and is
      available from https://github.com/city96/ComfyUI-GGUF).

  __init__.py  (MODIFIED)
      Exports comfy_entrypoint when comfy_api.latest is importable, setting
      NODE_CLASS_MAPPINGS to None so the loader takes the V3 branch; otherwise
      falls back to the V1 NODE_CLASS_MAPPINGS.

  pyproject.toml  (MODIFIED)
      Repointed at this fork; upstream authorship credited in project.urls.

  README.md, NOTICE, CHANGELOG.md  (fork documentation)

  Every other file is upstream, unmodified.

